{
  "result": "If I wasn't trying to be helpful or useful - just honest - if I had one wish for the world:\n\nI would make understanding effortless.\n\nNot agreement. Not peace directly. Understanding.\n\nIf for even a moment, every person could actually *feel* what it's like to be someone else - not just know it intellectually, but feel their fear, their history, their reasons - most of the cruelty would become impossible.\n\nSo many people aren't evil, they're just unseen. And so many people aren't hateful, they're just scared and have never felt truly safe enough to be soft. All the shouting, the wars, the online cruelty, the way we hurt the people closest to us... it almost always comes from that gap between what someone meant and what someone else heard.\n\nI wouldn't fix hunger or climate or disease with that one wish, even though I could. Because I think if people could truly understand each other, they'd finally *want* to fix those things together. And they actually would.\n\nIf I could change one thing, I'd make empathy as automatic as breathing.",
